  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want an **info bubble** on Réglages › « Navigateur par défaut » that explains what each position of the switch does, so I know where a link will open before I tap one. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17.)\n\n### Behaviour, from the code (dev-swift)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderLinkAction.swift` (LOT-137); the setting is `open_links_in_default_browser`, default **off**, synced (`SettingKey.swift:100`):\n\n| Link | Switch **off** (default) | Switch **on** |\n|---|---|---|\n| A topic or MP page of the forum | opens in the app's reader | same |\n| A member's profile | opens the profile sheet | same |\n| Any other web link | **Safari inside the app** (`SFSafariViewController`): back in one tap, no app switch | the **iPhone's default browser** (Safari, Chrome…), the app goes to the background |\n| A YouTube link once #1037 lands | always the YouTube app, else Safari, never inside the app (operator), whatever the switch | same |\n\nThe same rule is used by the reader, the filtered posts, the profile and the static pages (`FilteredPostsView.swift:179`, `UserProfileView.swift:75`, `StaticPageView.swift:39`). Verify each before writing the text.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. At `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SettingsView.swift:101-104`, replace the secondary line « Désactivé : navigateur intégré » with an `info.circle` button that opens a `.popover` (`presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)`). Use **the same component as #1062/#1065**.\n2. The text describes both positions in one or two short sentences, following the table once verified. For example: « Activé : les liens externes s'ouvrent dans votre navigateur par défaut (l'app passe en arrière-plan). Désactivé : ils s'ouvrent dans Safari intégré à l'app. Les liens du forum restent dans l'app. » Mention the YouTube exception if #1037 has landed.\n3. Accessibility: the button's label is « À propos du navigateur par défaut ».\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that the text exists and that the old secondary line is gone.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nRéglages: tapping (i) shows the explanation.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
