   "body": "Verified in the code (dev-swift), as asked. The table is right for the **reader** and wrong for the other three screens it names; the text follows the code.\n\n| Screen | Code | What a link does |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reader | `TopicReaderModel+Links.swift:12-19` | topic or MP page of the forum → the app's reader; a member's profile → the profile sheet; every **other** `http(s)` link → Safari inside the app (switch off) or the default browser (on). A forum page the router does not own (a list…) goes to the browser too, never into the reader with the session. |\n| Profile | `UserProfileModel.swift:151-154` | **every** `http(s)` link follows the switch, forum topic links included (« a browser, never the reader with the session », LESSONS 43). |\n| Filtered posts | `FilteredPostsView.swift:177-180` | **every** `http(s)` link follows the switch, forum topic links included: there is no reader there to open one in. |\n| Static pages | `StaticPage.swift:48-51` | same: « a browser, never the reader and never with the session ». |\n\nSo « forum topic and MP links stay in the app either way » holds **in the reader only**. The bubble says exactly that: « Désactivé : les autres liens s’ouvrent dans Safari, intégré à l’app. » / « Activé : ils s’ouvrent dans le navigateur par défaut de l’iPhone ; l’app passe en arrière-plan. » / « Dans le lecteur, les sujets, les MP et les profils du forum restent dans l’app, quel que soit le réglage. » No YouTube sentence: #1037 has not landed (`ReaderLinkAction` has no YouTube case).\n\nBehaviour is not changed. If a topic link tapped in the filtered posts or in a profile should open the reader, that is a separate behaviour change: say so and I open an issue. Implemented in PR #1064 (`Closes #1071`).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
